  "level": {
    "$comment": "Theme-stable 5-step ordinal scale (red -> orange -> gold -> green -> blue) for ranking a quantity where more/less reads as better/worse: benchmark scores, resource-heaviness, capability tiers. Formalizes a scale CI-Hub's onboarding/ai-setup already shipped independently (packages/frontend/src/modules/onboarding/components/ai-setup/levels.ts) — not a new design decision, a name for an existing one. Distinct from status (success/warning/info), which is binary-ish state, not a 5-point rank.",
    "red": {
      "hex": "#ef4444"
    },
    "orange": {
      "hex": "#f97316"
    },
    "gold": {
      "hex": "#f59e0b"
    },
    "green": {
      "hex": "#10b981"
    },
    "blue": {
      "hex": "#0ea5e9"
    }
  },
  "category": {
    "$comment": "Theme-stable categorical set for telling unrelated groups apart at a glance (marketplace app categories today) when there are more groups than --chart-1..5 covers. Not semantic — a category's hue carries no meaning beyond 'not the others'. Formalizes CI-Hub's onboarding CATEGORY_ACCENTS (packages/frontend/src/modules/onboarding/components/recommendations-step.tsx). Add new keys as new categories appear; never reuse a hue for two live categories.",
